@startuml reconcile
' Revision 2 (2026-10-12): distinguish admitted pending stop/retire continuation from observation-only holds.
title Companion to M-DP1 / M-DP2: service slices reconciliation (draft)
participant "Dispatcher core\nservice UID swarma-dispatcher" as D
database "Dispatcher-owned journal, effects,\ninput/agent/run records and claims" as J
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot; account ledger / stop evidence" as H
participant "Credential broker\nunprivileged; binding / grant / lease owner" as B
participant "Process evidence\nsupervisor service UID / executor agent UID" as P
D -> J : local lock: exclusive ownership/schema/replay; classify records; release lock
D -> D : publish valid recovery/control surface; forward admission separately gated
opt declared state loss / restore (§11.1)
  D -> J : external restore fence precedes visible restored bytes; coverage unavailable
  D -> H : reverse inventory created_by dispatcher accounts + surviving receipts
  D -> B : reverse inventory own bindings / tombstones
  D -> J : orphans retain identity/accounting; signed operator decision required
  D -> D : reopen only with independent coverage + external fence reconciliation
end
loop bounded per-record allocation / execution work (§7.1)
  D -> J : local lock: snapshot versions, intent and in-flight marker; unlock for calls
  D -> H : effect.observe original request_id / operation / canonical argument digest
  H --> D : one of six states; recorded includes result + current target state
  D -> H : observe generation and qualified start/termination receipts
  D -> B : effect.observe bind/unbind/binding replacement; original request_id / operation / digest
  B --> D : one of six states; unbind removal/tombstone evidence
  D -> P : observe supervisor registration / execution identity
  D -> J : local lock: revalidate record/daemon/controller fences; record observations; unlock
  alt relevant receiver observation unavailable or contradictory; required identity/fence evidence unsound
    D -> J : retain state and capacity; retry observation later\nnever relaunch or declare cleanup successful
  else stopping; observed pending for admitted exec.stop (including processes_remain)
    D -> H : continue original E-stop with identical canonical arguments\nrevalidate generation/current-execution and latest-receipt fences
    D -> J : retain claims; no absence or success until confirmed
  else retiring / cleaning; observed pending for admitted user.retire
    D -> H : continue original E-retire with identical canonical arguments\nrevalidate generation/current-execution fences; ordinary unbind already confirmed
    D -> J : retain UID/quota reservations; no removed state before full confirmation
  else other observation unknown
    D -> J : retain state and capacity; retry observation later\nnever relaunch or declare cleanup successful
  else provisioning; create effect unknown before query
    D -> J : apply R-OBS; rolled_back/not_recorded never automatic new create
  else provisioning; account present; bind known absent after query
    alt request still valid
      D -> B : revocation.check exact chains, context prepare
      alt not_revoked and other authority checks pass
        D -> B : resume only same admitted bind effect; no automatic new effect
      else revoked / unavailable
        D -> J : no forward effect; retain pending / authorized cleanup
      end
    else invalid authority/window
      alt ordinary allocation
        D -> J : retire only under §5.4; expiry needs trusted elapsed gate; confirm cleanup
      else standing allocation
        D -> J : retain pending; await operator-signed decision; no re-creation
      end
    end
  else idle; binding known absent; ordinary not expired or standing
    D -> D : fresh explicit authority needed for any new bind
    D -> B : revocation.check exact chains, context prepare
    alt authority valid and not_revoked
      D -> B : E-rebind only with explicit renewal consent/current chains\nno account recreation; binding replacement + old tombstone
    else authority gone / revoked / unavailable
      alt ordinary allocation
        D -> J : retire only under §5.4; expiry needs trusted elapsed gate
      else standing allocation
        D -> J : no forward execution; await operator-signed decision; no retirement
      end
    end
  else claimed; supervisor registration conclusively absent
    D -> J : mark execution claim absent; no later launch
  else launching; receipt unknown
    D -> J : wait for receipt/launcher answer; cancel also waits; never relaunch
  else started; supervisor known absent
    D -> H : exec.stop {same E-stop, generation, execution_id}
    H --> D : termination receipt only after quiet-period account-wide absence
    D -> J : record lost after confirmation
  else stopping; receiver recorded; termination receipt missing
    D -> H : continue same E-stop and canonical arguments; latest-receipt fence
  else supervisor survives replaced daemon
    D -> J : old daemon-instance writes refused; never adopt; reconcile historical effect/stop
  else direct operator retirement; unbind unconfirmed
    D -> J : retain/report durable broker-cleanup obligation
    D -> B : authorised E-unbind / observe retained removal tombstone
  else authorised credential renew-ahead on existing allocation
    D -> B : fresh revocation.check prepare; narrowed E-rebind binding replacement
    D -> J : same uid/generation; old tombstone; horizon update only after confirmation
  else retiring / cleaning; remaining authorised cleanup with known observations
    D -> B : repeat applicable unbind with same effect ID
    D -> H : retire only after unbind confirmed; same retire effect ID
    D -> J : applicable one-shot identity cleanup after retirement (§14)\nterminal only after all required confirmations
  end
end
note over D,J
  Controls after ownership/schema/replay/authentication; classify every record for forward readiness.
  Complete accounting + confined unknown retains local claims; unbounded uncertainty closes node.
  Maintenance/restore/hold remain global barriers. No fresh launch grant needed for observation.
  R-LOCK: never hold state lock on cross-service calls; per-record durable in-flight markers.
  Wait graph: state lock -> local journal/records; unlocked workers -> helper/launcher/broker.
  Bounded workers/sweep; cancel intent prompt; stale results cannot reopen admission/delivery.
  R-FATE user-manager §7; all old-instance supervisor writes fenced, no live adoption.
  Internal daemon sweep every minute (§7.2); absent/unready daemon refuses new admission.
  R-OBS: recorded -> known present/absent by current target state.
  rolled_back / not_recorded -> known absent for that effect only; never automatic new create.
  pending / unavailable -> unknown; contradictory -> contradictory.
  Missing/expired evidence is unavailable, never absence; read serialized with receiver journal.
  Only original receiver caller or operator may observe, including after initiating grant expiry.
  Standing: no expires_at or lifetime quota; sweep never expires it.
  Standing executions: no max_runtime quota or deadline, including after recovery.
  Sweep never stops them for runtime; ordinary executions keep 4 h / 12 h,
  and sweep stops them through exec.stop when their runtime deadline elapses (§7.2).
  R-OPERATOR: swarma-operator never hosts harness sessions; operator authority stays there.
  Signed operator records: operator device key on phone + biometric/content confirmation, or terminal password/content confirmation.
  Operator records from agent sessions refuse; command/signature formats unpublished (§§3.2, 16).
  swarma-observer reads dispatcher state without confirmation; no mutation authority.
  Standing retirement/re-creation requires operator-signed record (§5.4).
  An absent account never authorises automatic standing re-creation.
  Intent is journaled before every external effect (§4.1).
  R-OUTCOME receiver tables: unfinished stop/retire remains pending, not terminal refusal.
  Observed admitted pending stop/retire may continue; unavailable/contradictory stays observation-only.
  Continuation requires sound identity/fence evidence, not a completed termination/deletion receipt.
  Same-ID continuation uses identical arguments and current-execution fence; old success never signals.
  No authority-creating retry without fresh admission; unknown is never absence.
  F-25: bounded helper deletion batches yield shared lock; same E-retire, no early UID release.
  E-rebind only from authorised current chains, never wider; no seamless lease handoff claimed.
  R-TIME watermark max expiry / min not_before; no untrusted advance.
  Expiry deletion requires trusted time + boot-inclusive elapsed lifetime; downtime delays it.
  Refused cleanup stays pending; unknown is never known absent (§4.6).
  Keeper API and broker service UID spelling are unspecified in spec §§14, 3.1.
end note
